  "title": "Tab groups, toolbars, banners and nav menus are assets with an asset settings interface, right-click to settings",
  "profile": "all",
  "category": "Framework",
  "priority": "",
  "repo": "amberx-axf"
 },
 "said": {
  "text": "Looking at UI Review's row (Design packs, Whole apps, Screens and pages, Settings interfaces, Dialogs, Menus), which switches the list = a tab group: \"If it's a tab group, why can't I get to the tab group settings by right-clicking on it?\" ... \"Needs to be. Yeah, all tab groups are supposed to be assets. With a settings interface, that's also an asset.\"\n\nAddendum 1 (voice, Nov 4): \"Right now, I want to make sure that navigation menus, toolbars, banners, are all asset types, and they all have a settings interface, which is an asset, and we can get to their settings by right-clicking all of them.\"\n\nAddendum 2 (voice, Nov 4): \"Every asset type that has the settings interface, there's going to be a default settings interface for all, used by default. And then there will be another one that will make a customized one for every app. And by default, the custom one will be selected.\"\n\nAddendum 3 (voice, Nov 4, correction): \"No, actually, by default, it uses the default one.\"",
  "verbatim": true,
  "at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z",
  "source": "voice",
  "by": "Brett",
  "addenda": []
 },
